## Facts (`doc/plan/c016-worklog/diag-cpp-sample-cleanup-137.md` §교차언어 종료 결과)
The cpp and java runners report exit 137 / `TEARDOWN_FAILED` when a role process must be SIGKILLed at cleanup; the dotnet and
node runners print the completion marker and exit 0 even though a role was SIGKILLed, hiding a teardown defect (that is how a
Core close hang, D-089, went unnoticed in those languages). AGENTS §4: do not mask failures.

## What to do
1. In the dotnet and node runners, after the graceful stop deadline, treat any role that did not exit on its own (had to be
   SIGKILLed, or exited 137/-9) as a runner failure: non-zero exit, a clear line naming the role, no completion marker — the
   same semantics the cpp/java runners already have (`runner-common.sh` java: `Sample process <pid> exited during cleanup with
   status …`). Do not change timeouts; do not add retries.
2. Verify: run TicTacToe and Bingo for dotnet and node 1× each (they should still pass if teardown is clean on the current
   packages; if a role is SIGKILLed the runner must now fail — report that honestly with the role name, do not mitigate).
3. Contract tests that pin runner behaviour (node `test/contract/sample-*` runner tests; dotnet `SampleRegressionTests`) must
   stay green or be updated to the new failure semantics only.

## Deliverable
`doc/plan/c016-worklog/stage2-sample-runners-report-sigkill-summary.md`: diff per runner, results, BLOCKERS.
